<%#
# Url Form Partial

This partial renders an input element for URL.
By default, the input is a text box.

## Local variables:

- `f`:
  A Rails form generator, used to help create the appropriate input fields.
- `field`:
  An instance of [Administrate::Field::Url][1].
  A wrapper around the URL pulled from the database.

[1]: http://www.rubydoc.info/gems/administrate/Administrate/Field/Url
%>

<div class="block text-sm font-medium text-gray-700 mb-1">
  <%= f.label field.attribute, field.attribute.to_s.humanize, class: "block text-sm font-medium text-gray-700 mb-1" %>
</div>
<div class="field-unit__field">
  <%= f.url_field field.attribute, class: "block w-full px-3 py-2 rounded-md bg-white border border-secondary-300 shadow-sm focus:border-primary-500 focus:ring-primary-500 sm:text-sm" %>
</div>
